# Local-first product rules

- The device is the system of record for conversations, memory, attachments, agent history, and settings.
- An account does not upload chats. Signing in attaches local guest threads to that account and leaves them on the device.
- Guest mode is the full local app. The chat nav shows Login. Login unlocks cloud sync, Histeeria, and frontier models.
- Auto is the default intelligence mode. Best quality uses frontier models. Private / Offline stays on the device even when the network is up.
- Private mode never sends a turn to the cloud. A turn already answered on device is not resent. Auto may use a frontier model on a later turn only when the device is online and cloud-inference consent is already on.
- Cloud inference sends the context package for that turn only. It is a separate consent from sync. Sync off means the archive is not backed up.
- Do not queue an offline prompt for a silent cloud send. If no local model is prepared, explain the limit.
- Users do not pick GGUF files, parameter sizes, quantization, or GPU settings.
